  "curriculumPageSha256": "020ac8417039c722f95c734949f0b8e522ea75cc4fd7c467802b3ad28d6800b2",
  "curriculum": "The official curriculum for 2026–2027 and dated catalogue identify one 180 EC full-time degree with substantively identical English and Dutch tracks, so no language variant is selected for the generic target. Both first and second years comprise ten 6 EC courses. The third year has a 30 EC choice space followed by five 6 EC components. An internship is combined with electives. The thesis comprises distinct research and skills components worth 6 EC each.",
  "progression": "The normal sequence completes 60 EC in year 1, exceeding the current 48 EC binding-study-advice threshold. Calculus, linear algebra, probability, economics and programming support advanced mathematics, econometrics, machine learning and life insurance in year 2. Risk Theory and the research seminar precede the year-3 specialisation. The normal plan completes 150 EC before the final semester, when insurance accounting, stochastic life models, finance and the two thesis components occur. The preceding 2025–2026 regulations corroborate the 120 EC threshold for both separately coded thesis components and the internship-plus-electives arrangement. The 2026–2027 study page governs current structure; the earlier OER is used only as historical corroboration, not to assert a current threshold.",
